{"diagnosis": "TRAP: cpu trap asserted with tohost FAIL 0xdead instead of clean 256-word NOP fetch progress (see picosoc/picosoc.v:146 cpu instance, VERDICT FAIL 0xdead). Root cause is picorv32.v line 376 mem_done term (&mem_state || mem_do_rinst) asserting mem_done on mem_do_rinst alone without mem_xfer and &mem_state, so instruction fetch completes with invalid mem_rdata_latched and traps.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -375,3 +375,3 @@
 	wire mem_busy = |{mem_do_prefetch, mem_do_rinst, mem_do_rdata, mem_do_wdata};
-	wire mem_done = resetn && ((mem_xfer && |mem_state && (mem_do_rinst || mem_do_rdata || mem_do_wdata)) || (&mem_state || mem_do_rinst)) &&
+	wire mem_done = resetn && ((mem_xfer && |mem_state && (mem_do_rinst || mem_do_rdata || mem_do_wdata)) || (&mem_state && mem_do_rinst)) &&
 			(!mem_la_firstword || (~&mem_rdata_latched[1:0] && mem_xfer));
", "expected": "tohost PASS with no TRAP: cpu trap asserted, 256-word NOP sweep completes"}

